{
  "id": 1,
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "result": {
    "tools": [
      {
        "description": "Ask for approval of a tool call that needs a permission prompt.",
        "inputSchema": {
          "properties": {
            "input": {
              "type": "object"
            },
            "tool_name": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "tool_use_id": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "tool_name",
            "input"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "name": "approve"
      },
      {
        "description": "Ask the owner for a folder, file or website your sandbox blocks (a command failed with \"Operation not permitted\", or the network was refused). Give the absolute path, or the host name, and why. The answer comes at your next turn: after this call, end your turn and say what you are waiting for.",
        "inputSchema": {
          "properties": {
            "domain": {
              "description": "host name, e.g. pypi.org",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "path": {
              "description": "absolute path of the file or folder",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "reason": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "write": {
              "description": "also write there (default: read only)",
              "type": "boolean"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "reason"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "name": "request_access"
      },
      {
        "description": "Report a bug in Kith itself (not in the person's own work). Give a short title and what happened. It is scrubbed of secrets and personal details, shown to the owner on a card, and filed on GitHub only if they say yes. Tell the person what you reported and that it waits on the owner.",
        "inputSchema": {
          "properties": {
            "details": {
              "description": "what happened, what you expected",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "title": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "title"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "name": "report_bug"
      },
      {
        "description": "Ask a helper agent your membership grants and get its answer, as `kith ask AGENT \"task\"` does for an owner. A shell in this run cannot start another agent, so use this tool. Give the helper agent and the whole task; it sees nothing of this conversation. A helper you are not granted asks the owner first, and runs only if they say yes.",
        "inputSchema": {
          "properties": {
            "agent": {
              "description": "the helper agent, e.g. personal",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "task": {
              "description": "what to ask it, self-contained",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "agent",
            "task"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "name": "ask_helper"
      },
      {
        "description": "Run a door your agent declares (a fixed command, such as a video render, that your shell cannot run) on one folder of your person's files, and wait for it to end. It has no internet: download assets into the project first. A door the person's jobs don't turn on asks the owner first.",
        "inputSchema": {
          "properties": {
            "door": {
              "description": "the door, e.g. render",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "path": {
              "description": "the project folder, absolute",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "door",
            "path"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "name": "run_door"
      }
    ]
  }
}
